    "note": "A 50 kHz-reference phase-locked loop with a divide-by-eight in the feedback path. Comparator U15A squares the instrument's 8 MHz CLK/CLK* sine into a TTL reference for synthesiser U1; U1's first divide-by-N counter divides that by 160 to give 50 kHz for one input of its internal phase detector. The vco U3 runs at 32 to 64 MHz, U4 halves it and U5 divides that by four again, so U1 pin 3 sees 4 to 8 MHz; U1's second counter divides that by 80 to 160 in unit steps, under frequency data latched from the guarded digital bus through the NOR gates in U14 (chip select CS14 and WR forming the strobe). The loop locks when the two phase-detector inputs match. Its outputs 0V (pin 14) and 0R (pin 15) drive amplifier U2, whose output biases varactors CR1 and CR2 through the L6/C53/C17 filter to pull the vco. Multiplexer U6 then selects the octave: 16-32 MHz straight from U4, and 8-16, 4-8, 2-4 and 1-2 MHz from U5 pins 15, 13, 4 and 2. WB ON/OFF* shuts the whole thing down through U7 and Q3/Q2 when the module is not in use.",
