   "note": "Read all three lines at each frequency and check TP10's frequency in the same pass; §5-5 step 10 requires TP10 within 0.01% as well. The three lines are made by comparators in U7 from WB MUXA, WB MUXB and WB MUXC, which arrive from the digital control circuit on A5 (§2-218), so a pattern that is wrong on all three points at U7 or at P101 rather than at U6. Two oddities of the printed table are worth knowing: the 1.2 MHz and 2.0 MHz rows select the same 1-2 MHz filter (1.2 MHz is inside that octave), and the pattern is not a plain binary count -- the 4.0 MHz row sets B and C together while 8.0 MHz sets only C. The table is transcribed exactly as printed."
