   "note": "The gate on the whole assembly. WB ON/OFF* comes from the digital control circuit on the Wideband Output assembly (A5) through P101 and, when low, shuts down both the 8 MHz clock generator and the vco -- §2-219 says a comparator in U7 inverts it to turn Q3 on, which turns Q2 off and takes the -5 V supply away from U3. So a board that looks completely dead with no 8 MHz at TP1 and nothing at TP3 is the expected behaviour if this line is low, and the fault is then on A5. Check it before replacing anything here."
